<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hannibal</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hannibal Barca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hannibal Barca was a Carthaginian general who led the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. After crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> he won major victories over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, including at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cannae">Cannae</a>, but could not force Rome to surrender. He was defeated at Zama, later took part in Carthaginian government, and remains the most famous figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hannibal.jpg" alt="Hannibal" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fratelli Alinari · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hannibal_Barca_bust_from_Capua_photo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
